        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.37,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "Now to update the Signal value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 9.78,
          "en": "we still reach out to the property, to the counter property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.78,
          "end": 11.4,
          "en": "but we now don't update it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.4,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "by assigning a new value like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "or by incrementing it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 22.38,
          "en": "Instead, this counter property now contains a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.38,
          "end": 24.9,
          "en": "a writeable Signal to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "which means a Signal that can be changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "To update it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 32.61,
          "en": "you now have to call a method on that Signal object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.61,
          "end": 34.8,
          "en": "and Angular indeed gives you three methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.8,
          "end": 37.2,
          "en": "for updating Signal values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 40.593,
          "en": "It gives you a set method to set a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "It gives you an update method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 48.27,
          "en": "to set a new value based on an old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 51.45,
          "en": "And I'll get back to all these methods in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 53.7,
          "en": "And it gives you a mutate method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "to also update the value based on an old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 60,
          "en": "But again, I'll get back to these methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "and the differences between mutate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "and update in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "Here we could, for example, update the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "by calling update and by then passing a function to update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 74.37,
          "en": "because this update method needs such a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 76.83,
          "en": "You have to pass a function to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.83,
          "end": 80.37,
          "en": "And this function will automatically receive the old value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.37,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "so in this case, the old counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "because Angular will call this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "and it will pass the old value to this function for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 91.28999999999999,
          "en": "And then in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.28999999999999,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "you should return the new Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 97.773,
          "en": "In this case, old counter plus one, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "That's how you could update this counter Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "And of course, we can do the same thing down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.03,
          "en": "in the decrement method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.03,
          "end": 112.923,
          "en": "Here we just want to subtract one instead of add one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "And that's how we can update a Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 118.65299999999999,
          "en": "after creating it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 123.15,
          "en": "Now please note that actions is not a Signal yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.15,
          "end": 125.883,
          "en": "This will change later, but at the moment, it's not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.87,
          "end": 130.62,
          "en": "So with that, we're updating this Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.62,
          "end": 132.93,
          "en": "and we added this Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.93,
          "end": 134.58,
          "en": "But if you now save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.58,
          "end": 137.22,
          "en": "and you have your development server up and running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.22,
